rl":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-01-09T16:11:36Z","updated_at":"2015-12-09T10:08:48Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Joel Cooper (BitBucket: [joel_cooper](http://bitbucket.org/joel_cooper))**:\n\n---\n\nI experienced the same problem within emacs.  Many new issues were flagged as errors that were not in earlier versions of pylint.  I tracked it down to:\n\n```\n#!python\n\ndef Run():\n    if len(sys.argv) == 1:\n        print \"Usage: %s <filename> [options]\" % sys.argv[0]\n        sys.exit(1)\n    elif not osp.exists(sys.argv[1]):\n        print \"%s does not exist\" % sys.argv[1]\n        sys.exit(1)\n    else:\n        sys.exit(lint(sys.argv[1], sys.argv[1:])) # <-- This line\n```\n\nArgument 1 of sys.argv is the filename.  This causes the '--disable=C,R,I' option to be skipped (the default is only used if the options argument is empty).\n\nChanging the line to the following fixes the problem for me:\n\n```\n#!python\n\n        sys.exit(lint(sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2:]))\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/163172349/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pylint-bot","id":16198247,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTk4MjQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16198247?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pylint-bot/subs